    lesson: "Clinical image processing applies transparent operations to image data in support of visualization, measurement, or research. Begin with correct image identity, geometry, modality, and provenance. Intensity operations remap values; filters combine neighborhood information; segmentation assigns regions; spatial transforms map coordinates. Each operation can change interpretation or measurements. Keep the original, record parameters and software, inspect overlays and artifacts, and avoid treating an educational processing output as a diagnostic result.",
