    lesson: "An image is a sampled data structure plus an interpretation context. Pixels and voxels represent samples; spacing and orientation link them to physical coordinates. Grayscale and RGB are display encodings, while medical values may have modality-specific meaning. PNG, JPEG, and TIFF represent general image formats with differing compression and metadata; DICOM is a medical-imaging standard carrying pixel data and structured attributes. Resolution and noise both influence quality, but quality depends on the task. SNR compares signal magnitude with noise variability under a clearly stated definition.",
